    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi guys! I'm using numba 0.59.1 and this error still happens.\r\n\r\nThe following kernel signature works with no trouble:\r\n```python\r\n@numba.cuda.jit('int64[:], int64[:], int64[:], int32[:]')\r\ndef func(arr1, arr2, arr3, arr4):\r\n     ....\r\n```\r\nbut this fails:\r\n```python\r\n@numba.cuda.jit(['int64[:], int64[:], int64[:], int32[:]'])\r\ndef func(arr1, arr2, arr3, arr4):\r\n     ....\r\n```\r\nwith the error:\r\n```python\r\nTypeError: No matching definition for argument type(s) array(int64, 1d, C), array(int64, 1d, C), array(int64, 1d, C), array(int32, 1d, C)\r\n```\r\nwith the input being the same in both cases. \r\n",
