    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "One is a signature, the other is a list containing one signature. \r\n\r\n@essoca Your signature is for A-ordered arrays, not C-ordered, and there's some subtle legacy behaviour that allows you to get away with a single incorrect signature but not a list of incorrect signatures. Please open a thread on the [Numba Discourse](https://numba.discourse.group) if you need more assistance with this.",
